      "content": "Both approaches have merit, as a balanced curriculum can foster critical thinking while preserving shared civic values. Focusing solely on triumphs may oversimplify history, whereas emphasizing only injustices could neglect the role of progress and cooperation. The most effective strategy likely integrates narrative arcs that acknowledge historical struggles while highlighting how communities work together to address them. This dual focus helps students understand complexity without fracturing their sense of belonging.",
