      "role": "user",
      "content": "I hear you on the \"middle ground\" thing, but that feels like a way to avoid picking a side. If the goal is to teach kids how to be critical thinkers, why would we even suggest that a \"triumphs-only\" approach is a valid educational alternative? It seems like that approach is more about propaganda than teaching history. Can't we just admit that a curriculum prioritizing systemic realities is the only one that meets actual educational standards?",
